course: dictionary
lesson: 11620
title: Approving looks and nods
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a word has a feeling in it, the words around it show you what that feeling is. «Mum gave an approving nod when I tidied my room.» A nod is a small movement of the head, and the word approving tells you that Mum thinks the tidy room is good.
explain: «The teacher gave me an approving look for my neat handwriting.» Look at the clues: the teacher is pleased with the handwriting. So approving means showing that you think something is good or right.
explain: Approving can also be a verb, as in «The council is approving the new park.» Here it means officially agreeing to something. Check the meaning by putting your idea into the sentence: does «the council is officially agreeing to the new park» still make sense? If yes, you have it.
fact: Approving means showing that you think something is good or right.
fact: «An approving smile» shows that someone is pleased with what they see.
fact: «Nodded approvingly» means nodded in an approving way; approvingly is the adverb.
fact: Approving is also the -ing form of the verb approve, which can mean officially agreeing to something.
fact: Context clues such as smiled, nodded, pleased or proud can help you work out whether approving shows liking or agreeing.
exercise: «Dad gave me an approving smile when I finished my homework.» What does approving mean here? | Showing he is bored | Showing he is angry | *Showing he thinks it is good | Showing he is lost
exercise: «The judge nodded approvingly.» Find and copy the word that shows how the judge nodded. | the | nodded | judge | *approvingly
exercise: «The coach gave an approving look.» What does the look show? | Disappointment | Tiredness | Fear | *Approval
test: Lily's teacher gave an approving nod. What did the nod show? | Sadness | *Good opinion | Confusion | Hurry
test: Which meaning fits approving best? | *Showing that you think something is good or right | Showing that you are sleepy | Showing that you are lost | Showing that you are very hungry
exam: In «The mayor is approving the new bridge», what does approving mean? | Looking tired | Forgetting it | Dropping it | *Officially agreeing to it
